================================================================================
REVIEWER DISAGREEMENTS (not applied as suggested)
================================================================================

- A3 / B68. A3 suggested "status di soggiorno"; B68 suggested "titolo di soggiorno". One legal term is used: "titolo di soggiorno". "Status" is an English loan next to "statuto", which these articles already use for the articles of association.
- A4. "più di uno" does not emit the lexicon 1 that "una persona" does. The sentence is "più di una persona".
- A22. "1 volta" is not deleted. Korean 1회 is a counted 1. It sits in parentheses after the corrected sentence, in the FAQ and in the body.
- A25. Q16–Q20 were not turned into headings, and the U+200B lines were not removed.
- A33. The English row really is Easy | Difficult | Easy. That reading makes an economic dismissal sound like an easy outcome. The row stays, labelled as procedural complexity, with "nessun esito è assicurato" in the label.
- A39. The Hangul urls were not edited.
- B21. "fino all’importo del danno effettivo" would drop the counted 1. The cap stays "fino a una volta l’importo del danno effettivo". "una volta" is in the lexicon, so the checker still sees 1, and the phrase is no longer the glued "1 volta".
- B31. "cedere a titolo gratuito" contains "gratuito", which the Italian forbidden-token rule treats as a free-service claim (the only exemption is the denial "non dice che il primo colloquio è gratuito"). Both sites (body and checklist) say "cedere in omaggio".
- B59. The sentence already said "in linea di principio". Inserting it again would double it. FAQ and body are "in linea di principio ciascuna per 1/3".
- B66. "il primo ordine" is not parsed as 1. FAQ and body keep "l’ordine 1".
- B43 was not merged into one block.
- "visibilità garantita" was applied. It does not match the pack’s "garantiamo" / "garanzia di risultato" ban.

